116 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 117 0 R/Alt(Scatterplot of the V-Dem civil society index (x-axis) against the public sector corruption index (y-axis) for 179 countries in 2023. The points slope downward from the upper left to the lower right: countries with stronger civil societies have less corruption. The Arab Barometer countries are highlighted and labeled, with Palestine split into the West Bank and Gaza; most have civil society scores between 4 and 8 and corruption scores between 4 and 9. Tunisia has the lowest civil society score of the group, at about 3.8.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 441 0 R>>
endobj
