331 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 332 0 R/Alt(Point range plot showing the regression coefficient for volunteering (the difference in the percent of volunteers and non-volunteers who trust civil society organizations, controlling for age, gender, education, and income), with 95% confidence intervals, for seven Arab Barometer countries. Six of the seven estimates are positive, ranging from about 2 to 5 percentage points. Iraq and Tunisia, which is highlighted, have the largest estimates, about 5 points, and they are the only two confidence intervals that don't cross 0. Jordan is the only negative estimate, at about -4 points. Mauritania has the widest confidence interval.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[11]/Pg 444 0 R>>
endobj
